{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$id": "https://helmstudio.local/contracts/messages/cmd.media.job.schema.json",
  "title": "studio → a runner: one media job (a sequence's export, a video take's frame, from 1.48 thumbnails, from 1.79 a mux, or from 1.82 a bake)",
  "description": "From API 1.17 (contracts/README.md, Timeline: media jobs). Subject cmd.media.<host>.<env> (stream CMD, work queue; durable media-<host>-<env>, max_ack_pending 1, ack wait 60 s), Nats-Msg-Id <job_id>:1. `owner_id` = the user. Sent at once to the env studio chose (one whose hosts key has `media`). The runner works on it in a worker apart from runs and model jobs (ffmpeg on CPU or the media engine: no model, no GPU memory, no admission; it never counts as holding weights), sends `+WIP` every 10 s, checks KV `cancels` key <job_id> before it starts and at least every 2 s, publishes evt.media.status running, evt.media.progress, then one terminal status, waits for its ack, then acks the command. A redelivery starts over. From 1.79 a mux (contracts/README.md, Music and sound: Save with the video): the video's picture copied (H.264), the sound encoded as AAC 48 kHz stereo, cut or padded with silence to the video's length. Never bytes or URLs: inputs are object keys under u/<owner_id>/, outputs go under output_prefix. From 1.82 a bake (contracts/README.md, Magic: Send to Timeline): a short clip studio's graph renders from one or two takes (a Magic send's fade, wipe or dissolve between two shots, a lane's fade in or out, a shot's effects), conformed and verified as an export is.",
  "allOf": [
    {
      "$ref": "envelope.schema.json"
    }
  ],
  "properties": {
    "type": {
      "const": "cmd.media.job"
    },
    "version": {
      "const": 1
    },
    "job_id": {
      "$ref": "defs.schema.json#/$defs/uuid",
      "description": "the media job id"
    },
    "data": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "kind",
        "inputs",
        "output_prefix"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "kind": {
          "enum": [
            "export",
            "frame",
            "thumbs",
            "mux",
            "bake"
          ]
        },
        "inputs": {
          "type": "array",
          "minItems": 0,
          "maxItems": 1000,
          "items": {
            "type": "object",
            "required": [
              "key",
              "kind"
            ],
            "additionalProperties": false,
            "properties": {
              "key": {
                "$ref": "defs.schema.json#/$defs/objectKey"
              },
              "kind": {
                "enum": [
                  "video",
                  "image",
                  "audio"
                ]
              }
            }
          },
          "description": "every distinct object the job reads, once each (the runner downloads each into a 0700 temp dir); args name them by index. An export of empty slots only (black and silence) reads none; a frame job reads exactly one; (1.32) an audio take on an audio track is kind audio: a WAV (from 1.38 also an mp3 or an m4a), mixed as a video's sound is (resampled to target.sample_rate, stereo, gain, mute, at / in / out); (1.48) a thumbs job reads 1-20, each kind image (an image take's file or a video's poster); (1.79) a mux job reads exactly 2: inputs[0] the video (kind video), inputs[1] the sound (kind audio); (1.82) a bake job reads 1 or 2, each kind video or image"
        },
        "output_prefix": {
          "allOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "defs.schema.json#/$defs/objectPrefix"
            }
          ],
          "description": "export: u/<owner_id>/exports/<job_id>/ (export.mp4, export.poster.png, export.last.png); frame: u/<owner_id>/frames/<job_id>/ (frame.png); (1.48) thumbs: u/<owner_id>/thumbs/<job_id>/ (<i>.webp per input index); (1.79) mux: u/<owner_id>/muxes/<job_id>/ (mux.mp4, mux.poster.png, mux.last.png); (1.82) bake: u/<owner_id>/bakes/<job_id>/ (bake.mp4, bake.poster.png, bake.last.png, bake.thumb.webp)"
        },
        "export": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": [
            "timeline_id",
            "revision",
            "mode",
            "target",
            "frames",
            "samples",
            "video_bitrate",
            "args"
          ],
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "properties": {
            "timeline_id": {
              "$ref": "defs.schema.json#/$defs/uuid"
            },
            "revision": {
              "type": "integer",
              "minimum": 1
            },
            "mode": {
              "enum": [
                "copy",
                "conform"
              ],
              "description": "the plan's: copy = picture stream copy (concat demuxer), conform = re-encode; sound is re-encoded in both"
            },
            "target": {
              "type": "object",
              "required": [
                "width",
                "height",
                "fps",
                "rate",
                "sample_rate"
              ],
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "properties": {
                "width": {
                  "type": "integer",
                  "minimum": 16,
                  "maximum": 4096
                },
                "height": {
                  "type": "integer",
                  "minimum": 16,
                  "maximum": 4096
                },
                "fps": {
                  "type": "number",
                  "exclusiveMinimum": 0
                },
                "rate": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "pattern": "^[1-9][0-9]*/[1-9][0-9]*$",
                  "description": "the exact frame rate (24000/1001)"
                },
                "sample_rate": {
                  "enum": [
                    44100,
                    48000
                  ]
                }
              }
            },
            "frames": {
              "type": "integer",
              "minimum": 1,
              "maximum": 432000,
              "description": "the sequence's length in frames (the progress total; the output must be within one frame of it); at most 2 hours at 60 fps (an export is at most 2 hours: contracts/README.md, Timeline: export plan)"
            },
            "samples": {
              "type": "integer",
              "minimum": 1,
              "description": "frames × sample_rate × den / num: the sound's length in samples"
            },
            "video_bitrate": {
              "type": "integer",
              "minimum": 1000000,
              "maximum": 40000000,
              "description": "bits per second for {venc}"
            },
            "args": {
              "type": "array",
              "minItems": 1,
              "maxItems": 4000,
              "items": {
                "type": "string",
                "maxLength": 65536
              },
              "description": "ffmpeg's arguments after the program name, built by studio (the one filter graph implementation), with placeholders the runner substitutes: `{in:<n>}` = the local absolute path of inputs[n], `{list}` = the concat list it writes from `concat`, `{out}` = the local output file, `{venc}` = its own video encoder arguments (expands to several: README, Timeline: media jobs). The runner refuses (failure `invalid`) a list with an `-i` not followed by `{in:<n>}` or `{list}`, a codec value (`-c`, `-c:v`, `-c:a`, `-codec*`, `-vcodec`, `-acodec`) other than copy, aac, rawvideo or pcm_s16le outside `{venc}`, an output other than `{out}`, or a filter that opens a file or URL (movie, amovie)"
            },
            "concat": {
              "type": "array",
              "minItems": 1,
              "items": {
                "type": "integer",
                "minimum": 0
              },
              "description": "copy: the inputs (by index) in clip order for the concat list (`file '<path>'` lines, `'` written as `'\\''`)"
            },
            "expect": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": {
                "type": "object",
                "required": [
                  "input",
                  "stream"
                ],
                "additionalProperties": false,
                "properties": {
                  "input": {
                    "type": "integer",
                    "minimum": 0
                  },
                  "stream": {
                    "$ref": "defs.schema.json#/$defs/videoStream"
                  }
                }
              },
              "description": "copy: the facts studio planned with, per video input; the runner probes each download and, when any differs, runs conform_args instead (reporting mode conform and the reason)"
            },
            "conform_args": {
              "type": "array",
              "minItems": 1,
              "maxItems": 4000,
              "items": {
                "type": "string",
                "maxLength": 65536
              },
              "description": "copy: the conform arguments to fall back to (same placeholders)"
            }
          },
          "allOf": [
            {
              "if": {
                "properties": {
                  "mode": {
                    "const": "copy"
                  }
                }
              },
              "then": {
                "required": [
                  "concat",
                  "expect",
                  "conform_args"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "frame": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": [
            "at",
            "index"
          ],
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "description": "inputs[0] is the video: write that frame as PNG at the video's size",
          "properties": {
            "at": {
              "enum": [
                "first",
                "last"
              ]
            },
            "index": {
              "type": "integer",
              "minimum": 0,
              "description": "the frame number from 0 (last: the take's frames − 1)"
            }
          }
        },
        "bake": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": [
            "target",
            "frames",
            "samples",
            "video_bitrate",
            "args"
          ],
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "description": "(1.82) a bake: the export's conform with studio's own graph (the same placeholders and checks as export.args); the output has the target's size, rate and sample rate and is within one frame of `frames`",
          "properties": {
            "target": {
              "type": "object",
              "required": [
                "width",
                "height",
                "fps",
                "rate",
                "sample_rate"
              ],
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "properties": {
                "width": {
                  "type": "integer",
                  "minimum": 16,
                  "maximum": 4096
                },
                "height": {
                  "type": "integer",
                  "minimum": 16,
                  "maximum": 4096
                },
                "fps": {
                  "type": "number",
                  "exclusiveMinimum": 0
                },
                "rate": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "pattern": "^[1-9][0-9]*/[1-9][0-9]*$",
                  "description": "the exact frame rate (24000/1001)"
                },
                "sample_rate": {
                  "enum": [
                    44100,
                    48000
                  ]
                }
              }
            },
            "frames": {
              "type": "integer",
              "minimum": 1,
              "maximum": 14400,
              "description": "the clip's length in frames (at most 10 minutes at 24 fps)"
            },
            "samples": {
              "type": "integer",
              "minimum": 1,
              "description": "frames × sample_rate × den / num: the sound's length in samples"
            },
            "video_bitrate": {
              "type": "integer",
              "minimum": 1000000,
              "maximum": 40000000,
              "description": "bits per second for {venc}"
            },
            "args": {
              "type": "array",
              "minItems": 1,
              "maxItems": 4000,
              "items": {
                "type": "string",
                "maxLength": 65536
              },
              "description": "ffmpeg's arguments after the program name, built by studio (the one filter graph implementation), with placeholders the runner substitutes: `{in:<n>}` = the local absolute path of inputs[n], `{list}` = the concat list it writes from `concat`, `{out}` = the local output file, `{venc}` = its own video encoder arguments (expands to several: README, Timeline: media jobs). The runner refuses (failure `invalid`) a list with an `-i` not followed by `{in:<n>}` or `{list}`, a codec value (`-c`, `-c:v`, `-c:a`, `-codec*`, `-vcodec`, `-acodec`) other than copy, aac, rawvideo or pcm_s16le outside `{venc}`, an output other than `{out}`, or a filter that opens a file or URL (movie, amovie)"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "allOf": [
        {
          "if": {
            "properties": {
              "kind": {
                "const": "export"
              }
            }
          },
          "then": {
            "required": [
              "export"
            ],
            "not": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "required": [
                    "frame"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "required": [
                    "bake"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "if": {
            "properties": {
              "kind": {
                "const": "frame"
              }
            }
          },
          "then": {
            "required": [
              "frame"
            ],
            "properties": {
              "inputs": {
                "minItems": 1,
                "maxItems": 1
              }
            },
            "not": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "required": [
                    "export"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "required": [
                    "bake"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "if": {
            "properties": {
              "kind": {
                "const": "thumbs"
              }
            }
          },
          "then": {
            "properties": {
              "inputs": {
                "minItems": 1,
                "maxItems": 20,
                "items": {
                  "properties": {
                    "kind": {
                      "const": "image"
                    }
                  }
                }
              },
              "output_prefix": {
                "pattern": "/thumbs/[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12}/$"
              }
            },
            "not": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "required": [
                    "export"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "required": [
                    "frame"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "required": [
                    "bake"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "if": {
            "properties": {
              "kind": {
                "const": "mux"
              }
            }
          },
          "then": {
            "properties": {
              "inputs": {
                "minItems": 2,
                "maxItems": 2,
                "prefixItems": [
                  {
                    "properties": {
                      "kind": {
                        "const": "video"
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "properties": {
                      "kind": {
                        "const": "audio"
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "output_prefix": {
                "pattern": "/muxes/[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12}/$"
              }
            },
            "not": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "required": [
                    "export"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "required": [
                    "frame"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "required": [
                    "bake"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "if": {
            "properties": {
              "kind": {
                "const": "bake"
              }
            }
          },
          "then": {
            "required": [
              "bake"
            ],
            "properties": {
              "inputs": {
                "minItems": 1,
                "maxItems": 2,
                "items": {
                  "properties": {
                    "kind": {
                      "enum": [
                        "video",
                        "image"
                      ]
                    }
                  }
                }
              },
              "output_prefix": {
                "pattern": "/bakes/[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12}/$"
              }
            },
            "not": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "required": [
                    "export"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "required": [
                    "frame"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
